Detach upstream's build graph from sources no Jac build retains.

cpython-sources.txt is the single authority on which CPython files exist in
the extracted tree. Upstream's makefile still names a few of them as ordinary
prerequisites, which turns "stop shipping this file" into a build failure
rather than a smaller tree. Each hunk here removes one such reference so the
manifest alone decides.

Marked exclusions ("# path  # removed:") are a separate mechanism: those files
are restored for the build-only host, and compiler-bridge.patch detaches them
from the graph for the reduced runtime only. Pruned entries ("# pruned:") are
absent from both builds, so this patch applies unconditionally, and second:
compiler-bridge.patch carries zero-context hunks that match on line number
alone, so it has to see pristine ones.

Two constraints shape the context below, and an edit that ignores either one
still applies on macOS and fails the Linux build.

  No hunk takes context from a line compiler-bridge.patch removes first:
  Makefile.pre.in lines 2201-2207 and 2214-2216 in the pinned tree. That is
  why the ceval.o hunk carries a single line on each side.

  Trailing context is at least as long as leading context. GNU patch refuses a
  hunk with fewer suffix than prefix lines even at --fuzz=0, while the patch
  2.0 that ships with macOS accepts it, so an unbalanced hunk passes locally
  and rejects in CI.

PYTHON_OBJS, Python/ceval.o, Python/optimizer.o and the JIT recipe: tier 2 and
the JIT are compiled only when --enable-experimental-jit is passed. build.sh
never passes it, so configure leaves _Py_TIER2 and _Py_JIT undefined, and
optimizer_analysis.c, optimizer_symbols.c and jit.c are then empty translation
units. Dropping those three from PYTHON_OBJS lets the manifest prune them
together with the two generated case tables they include.

optimizer.c stays. Its outer #ifdef _Py_TIER2 has an #else that defines the
_PyDumpExecutors stub, which sysmodule.c calls unconditionally, so the object
is not empty and the source is not pruned; only its executor_cases.c.h
prerequisite goes, which it never actually includes. ceval.c likewise guards
its own executor_cases.c.h include, so there too only the prerequisite goes.
jit_stencils.h becomes unreachable once jit.o does, because configure leaves
JIT_STENCILS_H empty unless the JIT is on.

regen-executor-cases and regen-optimizer-cases keep naming pruned and
discarded sources, as regen-parser already does: no default target reaches
them.

build_all: gdbhooks copies Tools/gdb/libpython.py next to the interpreter for
test_gdb, and Programs/_testembed is an embedding test program. Neither is
installed, and no test suite is copied into the runtime.

altmaninstall/maninstall: the manual page lands under $(MANDIR), inside the
share tree that build.sh discards after install. It was written and deleted.

libinstall: Modules/xxmodule.c is a sample extension, named as a prerequisite
and never read by the recipe.

MODULE__SSL_DEPS: _ssl.c includes exactly one generated error table, chosen by
OpenSSL version. sources.json pins OpenSSL 3.5.8, so _ssl_data_35.h is the
only one compiled; the 1.1.1 and 3.0 tables survive as prerequisites alone.

